From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 07 Oct 2026 10:24:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: send the HE BSS info for each HE link

mac80211 keeps a separate configuration for each link of an MLD and
sets HE support only there; the default configuration of the
interface belongs to no link. The BSS info update tested HE support
in the default configuration, so the firmware got no HE basic
parameters (PE duration, TXOP RTS threshold, HE MCS and NSS limits)
for any link of an MLD.

Test the link that is updated. For a non-MLD interface the default
configuration is the only link, so nothing changes there.

Fixes: 807090b28661 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: prepare mt7996_mcu_add_dev/bss_info for MLO support")
Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -1379,7 +1379,7 @@ int mt7996_mcu_add_bss_info(struct mt799
 		mt7996_mcu_bss_txcmd_tlv(skb, true);
 		mt7996_mcu_bss_ifs_timing_tlv(skb, phy);
 
-		if (vif->bss_conf.he_support)
+		if (link_conf->he_support)
 			mt7996_mcu_bss_he_tlv(skb, vif, link_conf, phy);
 
 		/* this tag is necessary no matter if the vif is MLD */
